3. 養聲

廣東話：你最近聲音好沙哂，應該要多啲養聲。
English: Your voice has been hoarse lately, you should take care of your voice.

4. 票尾

廣東話：你記得唔記得，買飛機票嘅時候，要將票尾留返畀做收據。
English: Do you remember to keep the ticket stub when buying a flight ticket as a receipt?

5. hacker

廣東話：呢個網站被一個hacker入侵咗，個資料都被搶咗。
English: This website was hacked by a hacker, and the personal data was stolen.

6. 石斛蘭

廣東話：我家陽台上有咗一盆石斛蘭，佢哋會依附喺樹上面生長。
English: I have a pot of Dendrobium orchid on my balcony; they grow attached to trees.

7. 吊詭 (#矛盾、#悖論)

廣東話：佢哋講嘅話好吊詭，前面講一句，後面又講另一句。
English: What he said is very contradictory; he said one thing first and then another.

8. 吊詭 (似非而是、荒謬)

廣東話：佢哋話自己係清白，但行為卻好吊詭。
English: He claims to be innocent, but his behavior is absurd.

9. 各為其主

廣東話：呢個案件好複雜，因為各方各為其主，唔易達成協議。
English: This case is complicated because each party acts for their own interests, making it difficult to reach an agreement.

10. 軨蓋

廣東話：你買咗呢件軟蓋，好似一件呔軨。
English: You bought this jacket; it looks like a suit jacket.

11. 打哥夫

廣東話：我個朋友好鍾意打哥夫，每個禮拜都會去球場。
English: My friend is very keen on playing golf; he goes to the golf course every weekend.

12. 免揀

廣東話：呢間店係免揀嘅，你買咗嘢唔好揀返嚟。
English: This shop is no returns; once you buy it, you cannot return it.

13. 擺闊佬

廣東話：佢哋喺酒席上好擺闊佬，點咗好多菜。
English: He was very generous at the banquet, ordering many dishes.

14. 廣播劇

廣東話：我個媽媽好鍾意聽廣播劇，每日都會開收音機聽。
English: My mother loves listening to radio dramas; she turns on the radio every day to listen.

15. 錄影機

廣東話：你買咗一部新錄影機，用嚟攝影嘢。
English: You bought a new camcorder to use for filming.

16. 吟詩吟唔甩

廣東話：佢哋證據好充足，完全係吟詩吟唔甩。
English: His evidence is very solid; it is completely indisputable.

17. 佈道大會

廣東話：呢個禮拜有個教會佈道大會，我可以陪你去嗎？
English: There is a church evangelism meeting this weekend; can I accompany you?

18. 寫手 (#寫作 嘅人。)

廣東話：佢哋係一位著名嘅寫手，寫咗好多好書。
English: He is a famous writer who has written many good books.

19. 寫手 (代替他人寫作嘅人。)

廣東話：我唔會寫申請書，可以求一個寫手幫我寫㗎。
English: I don't know how to write an application letter; can I ask a ghostwriter to help me write it?

20. 代打 (#代替 另一人#打機。)

廣東話：我個朋友好鍾意打機，但冇時間，所以我幫佢代打。
English: My friend loves playing games but has no time, so I play on his behalf.

21. 茶碗

廣東話：呢個茶碗係日本茶道嘅道具，由陶瓷燒製而成。
English: This tea bowl is a Japanese tea ceremony utensil, made of pottery.

22. 茶隔

廣東話：你買咗一個茶隔，用嚟將茶葉同茶湯分開。
English: You bought a tea strainer to separate the tea leaves from the tea.

23. 只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈

廣東話：呢個制度好似「只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈」，權貴可以為所欲為，但我哋唔好講真話。
English: This system is like "only the officials can set fire, but the common people cannot light a lamp"; the privileged can do as they please, but we cannot speak the truth.

24. 獨唱

廣東話：佢哋好鍾意獨唱，喺卡拉OK房入面一個人唱好耐。
English: He loves singing solo; he sings very well alone in the karaoke room.

25. 快人快事

廣東話：佢哋係一個快人快事嘅人，講嘢直接，做嘢爽快。
English: He is a straightforward person; he speaks directly and acts efficiently.

26. 四腳獸

廣東話：你見過咗廁所外面嘅四腳獸嗎？好噁心。
English: Have you seen the "four-legged beasts" outside the restroom? It's disgusting.

27. 無米粥

廣東話：我哋現時只係煲無米粥，未有正式達成協議。
English: We are just talking preliminarily now; no formal agreement has been reached yet.

28. 義會

廣東話：過去時候，低下階層人哋唔好借錢，就會組織一個義會，邊個急需用錢就可以畀利息標會。
English: In the past, lower-class people who couldn't borrow money from banks would organize a "mutual aid society"; whoever urgently needed money could bid with interest to get the funds.

29. 榜文

廣東話：你見過咗貼喺榜上面嘅榜文嗎？
English: Have you seen the notices posted on the bulletin board?

30. MK名

廣東話：佢哋網上嘅MK名好特別，配咗好多意味不明嘅符號。
English: His online nickname is very special, with many meaningless symbols. [end of text]


